abstract: >
  A scanning holographic acoustic camera that uses a polargraph to
  move a microphone across the field of view while a lock-in amplifier
  measures the amplitude and phase of the acoustic signal. Phase-encoded
  color scatter plots and gridded interpolation provide real-time and
  post-processed holographic maps of the sound field.
